  "explains": "A line inside the arrow function of customersRouter.get(\"/:customerId/orders\", ...) in src/routes/customers.ts changes. The handler is written in the route call, outside every declaration, so the change is a module-level change of the file and the statement that holds the line is the route: GET /api/v1/customers/{customerId}/orders. The statement belongs to the router customersRouter (Router({ mergeParams: true }), which does not change the path), mounted by apiRouter.use(API_VERSION + \"/customers\", customersRouter) under app.use(API_PREFIX, apiRouter). The two other routes of the router are other statements and are not reached. The client calls customerOrdersUrl(customerId), /api/v1/customers/${customerId}/orders, with a parameter segment that fits {customerId}; fetchCustomerOrders calls it, so the http edge goes to the route and CustomerScreen, mounted at /customers/:customerId, is reached (it calls fetchCustomer too, a different URL).",
